WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:04.529
Welcome to Atlantis Expedition!

2
00:00:04.529 --> 00:00:10.497
In this video you will learn how to play by watching a real game against the computer, step by step.

3
00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:16.903
You run a diving company, racing a rival company to the treasures of the sunken city.

4
00:00:16.903 --> 00:00:21.427
Over ten tides you hire divers, build submarines and send them on dives,

5
00:00:21.427 --> 00:00:24.564
and every dive is a roll of a twenty-sided die.

6
00:00:24.564 --> 00:00:28.164
When the season ends, the company with the most points wins.

7
00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:33.004
This is the home page.

8
00:00:33.004 --> 00:00:39.100
The Game lobby button takes you back to all the board games, and the music button turns the music on or off.

9
00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:44.804
First pick your opponent: the computer, or two players sharing this device.

10
00:00:44.804 --> 00:00:47.700
Online play arrives when the game launches.

11
00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:54.111
Name your company, then choose how strong the computer is. Easy takes wild risks.

12
00:00:54.111 --> 00:01:00.235
Hard works out the odds of every move, and Brutal also starts with a bigger sub and an extra diver.

13
00:01:00.235 --> 00:01:01.936
We will take on Hard.

14
00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:09.293
Then pick who starts. We will go first. Below that are the rulebook and your game history.

15
00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:18.575
Across the top is the tide tracker. The season lasts ten tides, one round each.

16
00:01:18.575 --> 00:01:24.607
The glowing pip marks tide six, when the Heart of Atlantis, the greatest prize of all, is sighted.

17
00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:28.479
Next to it is the sea forecast.

18
00:01:28.479 --> 00:01:33.173
Every tide has one sea event that lasts the whole tide, for both companies.

19
00:01:33.173 --> 00:01:37.271
Tide one is always Calm seas: every dive roll gets plus one.

20
00:01:37.271 --> 00:01:43.928
You can also see the next one coming: Treasure rumors, when every successful dive finds two extra pearls.

21
00:01:43.928 --> 00:01:48.147
The strip below the companies spells out exactly what the event does.

22
00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:56.385
These are the two companies, with their pearls, gold, divers, subs and points so far.

23
00:01:56.385 --> 00:02:00.739
We start with seven gold, one Minnow submarine and one rookie diver.

24
00:02:00.739 --> 00:02:03.635
A Hard computer starts with three extra gold.

25
00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:07.449
This is the chart of Atlantis.

26
00:02:07.449 --> 00:02:13.531
The harbor is at the top, and five rows of dive sites lead down to the Heart of Atlantis at the bottom.

27
00:02:13.531 --> 00:02:16.661
Each row is harder, and richer, than the one above.

28
00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:24.396
Each site shows its level in stars, its haul of pearls, and its hazards, like sharks or currents.

29
00:02:24.396 --> 00:02:28.081
The percentage is your best chance of success there right now.

30
00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:32.060
Only the top row is charted at the start.

31
00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:36.968
A site further down is uncharted until someone explores a site with a route to it,

32
00:02:36.968 --> 00:02:40.845
and diving there costs minus three. The lines show the routes.

33
00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:46.063
On the right is your company: your fleet of subs, and your crew.

34
00:02:46.063 --> 00:02:50.992
Every diver has a skill, a depth they are trained for, and sometimes a specialty.

35
00:02:50.992 --> 00:02:55.701
Our rookie, Finn, has one star of skill, and is trained only for the Shallows.

36
00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:02.911
Below the chart is the dive hall. Both companies hire from the same five divers.

37
00:03:02.911 --> 00:03:06.581
Every diver gets one gold cheaper for each tide they wait,

38
00:03:06.581 --> 00:03:10.331
and the one who has waited longest leaves at the end of the tide.

39
00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:17.468
Next to it are this game’s three commissions: Deep-sea pioneers, Flagship, Hot streak.

40
00:03:17.468 --> 00:03:20.648
The first company to complete each one scores its points.

41
00:03:20.648 --> 00:03:24.781
Relics, found at the trickier sites, score in sets of different kinds.

42
00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:30.539
And the captain’s log records every move, from both companies.

43
00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:37.129
On your turn you take exactly one action: dive, hire a diver, use the shipyard,

44
00:03:37.129 --> 00:03:41.547
go on a salvage run, or end your tide. Then it is the rival’s turn.

45
00:03:41.547 --> 00:03:44.784
Each sub and each diver can go out once per tide.

46
00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:51.313
Two of the top-row sites have sharks, and nobody in our company is ready for them,

47
00:03:51.313 --> 00:03:56.413
so a dive there would get minus three. Maren, a shark wrangler, is ready for sharks.

48
00:03:56.413 --> 00:04:00.803
She costs four gold to hire, and one gold in wages every tide.

49
00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:06.268
That used our move, so now the rival takes its turn.

50
00:04:06.268 --> 00:04:09.975
Its moves pop up at the bottom of the screen, and go in the log.

51
00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:15.597
On its turn, the rival hired Barnaby, a rookie diver, for 2 gold.

52
00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:20.500
Now let’s dive. Click a site on the chart to open the dive planner.

53
00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:23.503
We’ll try Coral Gate Reef, worth four pearls.

54
00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:26.452
First choose a submarine.

55
00:04:26.452 --> 00:04:32.213
Or, with no sub at all, up to two divers can swim out from the dive boat, at minus three.

56
00:04:32.213 --> 00:04:37.392
We’ll take our Minnow. It has one seat, so the planner picks the best crew for it: Maren.

57
00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:43.679
Here is the most important part: the exact number the die has to show.

58
00:04:43.679 --> 00:04:45.643
The target at this site is six.

59
00:04:45.643 --> 00:04:51.788
Maren’s skill adds one, the calm sea adds one, and she is ready for the sharks, so there is no penalty.

60
00:04:51.788 --> 00:04:56.561
Six, minus two, means we need four or higher on the twenty-sided die.

61
00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:04.135
The track lights up every winning face of the die. That’s an 85 percent chance.

62
00:05:04.135 --> 00:05:09.889
A natural twenty always succeeds, and a natural one always fails, whatever the bonuses.

63
00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:16.068
Before you commit, this box tells you exactly what happens if the dive fails.

64
00:05:16.068 --> 00:05:21.211
We are ready for every hazard here, so a normal failure just comes home empty-handed.

65
00:05:21.211 --> 00:05:24.235
Only a natural one could still let the sharks strike.

66
00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:27.419
Let’s dive!

67
00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:33.691
The die shows ten. That is four or higher, so the dive succeeds!

68
00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.599
We bring up four pearls and two gold.

69
00:05:36.599 --> 00:05:41.827
We are also the first company to finish an easy expedition, which is worth two points.

70
00:05:41.827 --> 00:05:45.725
And the routes below this site are now charted, for both companies.

71
00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:49.617
Maren also gains experience.

72
00:05:49.617 --> 00:05:55.948
After two successful dives, a diver is promoted: plus one skill, and trained one zone deeper.

73
00:05:57.200 --> 00:06:02.208
The site now carries our flag, and nobody can dive it again. Back to the rival.

74
00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:06.152
This time, the rival built a Minnow for 3 gold.

75
00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:10.604
Our Minnow and Maren have been out this tide, but Finn is still ready.

76
00:06:10.604 --> 00:06:15.271
With no sub, he can swim out from the dive boat. Let’s try Kelp Garden.

77
00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:19.777
This one is riskier. Swimming costs minus three,

78
00:06:19.777 --> 00:06:25.155
and Kelp Garden has currents that nobody on the dive is ready for: another minus three.

79
00:06:25.155 --> 00:06:29.395
So Finn needs ten or higher. That’s a 55 percent chance.

80
00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:38.217
The fail box warns us: if it fails, the current costs three gold of gear, and Finn has to rest next tide.

81
00:06:38.217 --> 00:06:39.897
Let’s take the chance.

82
00:06:41.240 --> 00:06:43.155
A two. The dive failed.

83
00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:47.505
The dice screen tells you exactly what happened: the currents struck,

84
00:06:47.505 --> 00:06:50.359
because nobody on the dive was ready for them.

85
00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:58.097
Below it, the penalty box lists every cost: three gold, and Finn is resting and can’t dive next tide.

86
00:06:58.097 --> 00:07:03.411
He’s back on tide three. And there is a small consolation: the next dive at this site,

87
00:07:03.411 --> 00:07:06.712
by either company, gets plus one from what was learned.

88
00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:12.807
Over to the rival again.

89
00:07:12.807 --> 00:07:16.876
Its dives get the same dice screen, so you always see what it rolled.

90
00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:22.616
This time, the rival tried Old Harbor Docks, but rolled a 3 and failed.

91
00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:26.729
We have nobody left who is ready, so we end our tide.

92
00:07:26.729 --> 00:07:30.699
The rival can keep going on its own until it ends its tide too.

93
00:07:30.699 --> 00:07:32.869
Watch it use the rest of its crew.

94
00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:40.305
Once both companies have ended the tide, the tide report pops up.

95
00:07:40.305 --> 00:07:45.491
It shows the new sea event, Treasure rumors, and everything that happened between the tides.

96
00:07:45.491 --> 00:07:49.780
Each company collected four gold, and paid every diver’s wages.

97
00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:51.844
A diver you can’t pay quits.

98
00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:59.604
The dive hall changed too: the diver who had waited longest left, new divers arrived,

99
00:07:59.604 --> 00:08:02.635
and everyone still waiting got one gold cheaper.

100
00:08:02.635 --> 00:08:07.408
And the first move alternates every tide, so this time the rival goes first.

101
00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:14.272
Let’s start tide two, and see what the rival does first.

102
00:08:14.920 --> 00:08:20.504
Going first, the rival dived at Amphora Field and succeeded, bringing up 5 pearls.

103
00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:26.000
In our company panel, Finn is resting this tide, and his card shows it.

104
00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:28.809
The shipyard builds submarines.

105
00:08:28.809 --> 00:08:33.461
Bigger subs carry more divers, reach deeper sites, and add to every roll.

106
00:08:33.461 --> 00:08:37.111
You can rebuild a sub as a bigger model by paying the difference,

107
00:08:37.111 --> 00:08:40.141
and fit subs with equipment, like a shark cage,

108
00:08:40.141 --> 00:08:43.144
that makes one hazard safe for everyone aboard.

109
00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:50.075
A Barracuda costs six gold, and we don’t have enough yet, so we’ll save up.

110
00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:58.052
When there is no dive worth the risk, a salvage run is a safe way to earn gold: one gold, plus one per diver.

111
00:08:58.052 --> 00:09:01.951
No dice and no danger. We’ll send the Minnow out with Maren.

112
00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:09.124
Everything is explained in the rulebook, always one click away from the Rules button at the top.

113
00:09:09.124 --> 00:09:12.212
It’s laid out like a real rulebook, in chapters.

114
00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:18.828
How a season plays walks through a whole tide, and exactly what happens between the tides,

115
00:09:18.828 --> 00:09:21.105
step by step, with an example.

116
00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:26.419
Diving explains the number you need, and every bonus and penalty.

117
00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:33.365
Hazards and penalties lists what each hazard does when a dive fails, both with a sub and when swimming.

118
00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:39.847
Divers, subs and fittings shows every kind of diver, with their skill, depth, specialty,

119
00:09:39.847 --> 00:09:42.700
price and wage, and every sub and fitting.

120
00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:48.052
The chart and the sea covers routes, depths and every sea event.

121
00:09:48.052 --> 00:09:51.609
And scoring and winning tells you how the points are counted.

122
00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:55.233
Let’s skip ahead to the end.

123
00:09:55.233 --> 00:10:01.735
The season ends after tide ten, or at the end of the tide in which someone finds the Heart of Atlantis.

124
00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:07.767
Points come from pearls, two points for each level of expedition you finished first,

125
00:10:07.767 --> 00:10:12.419
relic sets, commissions, and one point for every four gold left over.

126
00:10:12.419 --> 00:10:15.827
The winner is revealed with the scorecard, row by row.

127
00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:22.344
From here you can look back at the chart, play again, or see your game history.

128
00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:27.145
Remember: check the number you need before every dive,

129
00:10:27.145 --> 00:10:32.459
cover the hazards with the right divers or fittings, and keep an eye on the sea forecast.

130
00:10:32.459 --> 00:10:37.623
Your game saves as you play, and you can keep several going from Your games in the game lobby.

131
00:10:37.623 --> 00:10:39.623
Good luck, and happy diving!

